---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Independent website support"
  description="Presence Web Services is a new independent business supporting local websites and Google profiles, with direct communication, agreed work and client-owned accounts."
>
  <PageIntro
    title="Independent website support, with a direct point of contact."
    description="Presence Web Services is a new independent service for businesses in Northern Ireland and across the UK. You deal directly with the person responsible for the work."
  />
  <section class="container about-editorial">
    <div class="about-opening">
      <h2>Why Presence exists</h2>
      <p class="large-copy">
        A business owner may know their website needs attention without having time to investigate
        every outdated page, inconsistent listing or missing enquiry.
      </p>
      <p>
        Presence takes on that work. The starting point is a conversation about the business: which
        services you want to promote, where customers come from and what information they need
        before contacting you.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those details affect the recommendation. A garage may need clearer service information. A
        landscaper may need to explain its coverage area before asking for a quote. Neither problem
        is solved by sending an automated report without following it up.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="about-context">
      <h3>Who the service is for</h3>
      <p>
        Trades, independent garages, landscaping, detailing, cleaning and other service businesses,
        including businesses in Belfast and elsewhere in Northern Ireland.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can ask for help with an existing site, a new website or your Google business
        information.
      </p>
      <a href="/services/" class="inline-link">
        See the work we can take on
      </a>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <section class="relationship-section">
    <div class="container relationship-layout">
      <div>
        <h2>How client work is handled</h2>
        <p>
          We agree what needs doing, explain the cost and keep a record of the changes. If something
          needs your input or a separate quote, we discuss it.
        </p>
      </div>
      <dl class="relationship-details">
        <div>
          <dt>You approve the priorities</dt>
          <dd>
            The proposal should explain what is included and what needs further assessment. Your
            knowledge of the business helps decide which changes are worth making.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>You can ask what changed</dt>
          <dd>
            Updates explain the work completed and what still needs attention. Where figures are
            available, we distinguish website activity from genuine enquiries and confirmed jobs.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Your accounts stay in your name</dt>
          <dd>
            You retain ownership of your website, domain and Google Business Profile. We agree the
            access needed and use delegated permissions where the platform supports them.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section container about-limits">
    <h2>A practical limit to what can be promised</h2>
    <div>
      <p>
        Presence can improve approved content, maintain supported systems and check that contact
        routes work. Google decides its own rankings and profile policies, and customers decide whom
        to hire.
      </p>
      <p>
        The aim is to help your online presence bring in enquiries, bookings and sales. We evaluate
        the changes with the information available, without guaranteeing those outcomes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="container page-next-step">
    <a class="inline-link" href="/services/">
      Explore the services
    </a>
    <a class="inline-link" href="/pricing/">
      See the starting prices
    </a>
  </div>
</Layout>
